Man! This Film Theory episodes are easy

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:43.260
OK!

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:43.760
So

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:46.160
Obviously, it's not as clear-cut as that

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:47.600
Eddard Stark is

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:48.840
Well, WAS

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:50.120
a pillar of virtue

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:51.840
I don't care how much junk

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:52.980
Wylla was carrying

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:54.140
in her trunk

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:55.220
Ned, was a type of man

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:57.060
who always stayed true to his vows,

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:58.500
to what was just.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.640
This is a guy who would trade his head

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:01.600
for his honour

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:02.320
LITERALLY

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:03.080
In Season One

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:05.160
we see him willing to die of starvation

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:06.200
in a prison cell

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:07.300
because he won't lie

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:08.960
about who the next king of the realm

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:09.760
rightfully is.

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:11.060
Eddard just isn't the type

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:13.600
of guy who would dishonor his wife like that

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:15.380
and pulling a page from reading rainbow

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:17.460
"You don't have to take my word for it"

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:19.380
King Robert's brother, Stanis

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:21.120
backs me up here in Season Five

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:24.400
saying that "Bedding a tavern whore wasn't Ned Stark's way"

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:25.680
and look at what Ned does

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:28.140
when Robert presses him to talk about Wylla

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:29.820
He nearly shuts down

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:31.840
with agony clearly in his eyes

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:34.540
refusing to speak anything but her name

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.740
This is a man who wouldn't've been able cheat on his wife even if he wanted to.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:40.800
Clearly! He's LYING!

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:42.020
You see loyal theorists

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:43.220
Jon Snow's mother

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:44.800
isn't some naughty nurse

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:46.740
or random tavern wench

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:47.520
but, instead

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.360
Ned's deceased sister

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:50.600
Lyanna Stark

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:51.620
Huu ho! Huu ho!

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:52.480
When I put it that way

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.300
it makes it sounds waaaay worse

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:55.580
Get your minds out of the gutter

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:58.000
This isn't a Circe-Jaime Situation

00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:59.580
STOP TYPING YOUR RAGE COMMENTS

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:02.160
Ned isn't an Incestious Necrophiliac

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:02.660
No!

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:03.780
My theory is that

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:04.280
Ned

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:05.960
isn't Jon's parent at all

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:08.400
that Jon's mother is Lyanna Stark

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.480
and that the father is actually

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:11.980
Rhaegar Targaryan

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:13.480
Now, if you've never seen the show

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:14.340
you're probably asking

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:14.940
Who's that??

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:16.160
and if you have seen the show

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:17.380
you're probably still asking

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:18.120
Who's that??

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:19.000
Because, seriously?

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:19.800
Who is that?

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:21.740
There's so many darn characters in the show

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:24.380
whose names are impossible to remember

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:25.340
Seriously!?

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:26.200
Roose Bolton!?

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:29.920
I mean who took notice of that guy before the end of Season Three? Amirite?

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:30.420
Okay!

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:31.720
So, who is Rhaegar?

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:32.960
outside of being the guy

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.480
whose name is literally impossible to type correctly

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:35.980
Well,

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:39.940
he's probably the most important character we'll never meet on the show

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:41.080
considering he's dead

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:41.580
But

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:43.380
we do know a lot about him already

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:45.960
He was Daenerys Targaryen older brother

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:48.100
and Heir to the throne of Westeros

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:50.540
We also hear in bits and pieces throughout Season One

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:52.220
that he kidnapped and raped Lyanna

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:54.100
and that Robert, who is engaged to her

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:56.600
started a war called "Robert's Rebellion"

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:57.260
to bring her back

00:05:57.260 --> 00:05:58.680
At the end of the rebellion,

00:05:58.680 --> 00:05:59.960
he ends up killing Rhaegar

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.980
but when they try to rescue Lyanna, she's already dying.

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:04.620
Lying in a bed of her own blood

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:05.760
But beyond Lyanna,

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:08.420
Rhaegar's death actually had huge repercussions

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:11.760
Resulting in the Tragaryan family being ousted from the throne

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:14.280
Daenerys and her brother having to flee the realm

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:16.480
and Robert Baratheon becoming King

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:18.800
So a pretty big deal for a guy that we've never met

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:20.920
So, what makes me say that we've been lied to

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:24.240
when that Jon Snow's parents are two characters that are already dead

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:25.500
and that we'll never meet

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:26.380
Let me explain,

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:28.260
although there have been hints here and there

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:31.460
Last week's episode actually gives us the strongest clue

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:34.280
we've yet seen on the show, confirming this theory

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:35.700
There's a crucial scene

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:37.980
that takes place in the crypts below Winterfell

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:39.940
Between Ned's e ldest daughter, Sansa

00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:42.420
and the sleaziest guy in the Kingdom of Westeros

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:43.600
Lord Baelish
*Booing Sound*

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:45.900
While they walk through the Hall of Fallen Starks

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:47.420
Sansa mentions that her father

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:49.600
never talk about a sister, Lyanna

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:51.700
and that others said that she was quite beautiful

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:53.160
This prompts Lord Baelish

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:56.240
to tell a story about the only time he ever saw Ned's sister.

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:57.400
It was at a Great Tournament,

00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:59.980
where everyone who is anyone was in attendance.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:02.480
Basically, it was like Westeros' Coachella

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:03.540
At the end of the tournament,

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:06.080
it was Rhaegar Targaryen who stood victorious

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:09.100
and as his prize, he was given a crown of blue roses

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:13.500
to give to the woman he believe to be the most beautiful in all of the Seven Kingdoms

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:15.620
It's a weird prize, but hey go with it

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:16.360
So, of course

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:18.220
everyone expected him to give it to his wife

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:19.340
Ellia Martell

00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:21.420
cuz' you know. It's HIS wife!

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:23.340
But he actually rode past her

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:24.620
to give the crown to...

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:25.420
You guessed it!

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:26.600
Lyanna Stark

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:27.120
Man!!

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:31.060
That had to be an awkward horseride back to the old stronghold. Right?

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:32.080
Shortly thereafter,

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:34.880
he kidnaps her and well we know the rest of the story

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:35.380
Or!?

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:35.880
Do we?

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:41.100
Did this guy really just kidnapped, raped and killed Lyanna because he thought she was pretty?

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:41.960
Something tells me,

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:45.480
you don't romantically and chivalrously give a crown of flowers to a girl,

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:48.020
if that's what you're planning to do a few weeks later

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:50.340
and honestly, i'm not the only one to think so

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:53.740
Sure, Robert Baratheon may badmouth Rhaegar on the show

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:56.200
but everyone else gives the guy glowing reviews

00:07:56.200 --> 00:08:00.720
Ser Jorah praises the late prince when he discusses Rhaegar with his sister, Daenerys

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:03.100
"Rhaegar fought valiantly,

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:04.460
Rhaegar fought nobly,

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:06.500
and Rhaegar died."

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:09.860
Ser Barristan Selmy, one of the noblest and most honorable people on the show

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:11.140
behind Ned Stark.

00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:15.600
Eagerly tells stories about how considerate and generous Rhaegar was

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:16.860
"Rhaegar never liked killing,

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:17.800
he loved singing"

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:19.580
"And what did you do with the money?"

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:29.580
Even Ned

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:31.340
has nothing but kind words

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:32.320
to say about to him in the books

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:33.520
Which is odd

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:34.840
when you're referring to the man

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:36.740
whose supposedly stole your sister

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:38.900
and had a direct hand in her death

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:41.340
Isn't it much more likely that this kidnapping story

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:44.300
is simply a cover for two kids who fell in love

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:46.740
and did something incredibly romantic

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:48.520
and incredibly stupid

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:49.820
by running away together?

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:51.340
We get an additional detail in the book,

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:53.560
that's after the supposed kidnapping

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:58.180
Rhaegar hides Lyanna away in a place named the "Tower of Joy"

00:08:58.320 --> 00:08:59.040
Really???

00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:00.680
The Tower of Joy?

00:09:00.860 --> 00:09:02.320
Subtle much? RR?

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:03.280
Seriously though,

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:07.440
these guys are fighting a war for him and he's hanging out in the Belfry of Banging?

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:08.880
The Minaret of Minaj?

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:10.700
The Parapet of Pleasure?

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:12.120
After Rhaegar's death,

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:17.100
the story we know is that Ned raises up the Tower of Titillation to free Lyanna,

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:21.160
only to find her dying in a bed of blood with her last words being

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:22.260
"Promise me, Ned"

00:09:22.900 --> 00:09:23.840
Now think about this,

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:24.580
a bed of blood?

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:27.400
Yes, it could be Rhaegar killing the girl.

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:30.560
But childbirth, can also be a pretty messy business

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:33.020
Then, she asks Ned to make a promise?

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:36.180
Could it be perhaps a promise to raise her newborn child?

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:37.660
Or to take it one step further

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:42.200
To keep the child safe by keeping his true parentage secret

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:48.540
I mean, you know, Robert would totally freak out if his beloved fiancee had a baby with another man

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:53.140
Robert just started with a rebellion against a royal dynasty in an attempt to get her back.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:54.940
"Oh sorry, we we're inlove"

